text:
Maya Chen: quick heads-up — opened PR to move per-model feature flags into k8s ConfigMaps and wire secrets with sealed-secrets. link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/421
Cheng Li: thanks! can you summarize rollout plan? will this trigger rolling deploys?
Maya Chen: plan is terraform-managed ConfigMap + annotation checksum so TF apply updates annotation -> deployment template change -> rollout. early test looked OK but want eyes on PR.
Samir Patel: fwiw, we saw race conditions last time when helm + tf touched same deployment. are we fully tf-driven here?
Maya Chen: yes TF-only for this change. keeping helm out of the loop for these flags.
Lucia Gomez: big question: one ConfigMap containing JSON for all models, or separate ConfigMap per model? tradeoffs: blast radius vs k8s API churn.
Cheng Li: separate per-model reduces blast radius. but with ~200 models API pressure might spike. maybe group by product/owner.
Samir Patel: +1 group-by-owner. also watch etcd size if flags get large (long JSON).
Infra SRE: notes: to trigger rollout reliably use checksum on spec.template.metadata.annotations. example Terraform pattern we use:
```
locals {
  flags_json = jsonencode(var.model_flags)
  cfg_checksum = md5(local.flags_json)
}
resource "kubernetes_config_map" "model_flags" {
  metadata {
    name = "model-flags-${var.owner}"
    annotations = {
      "checksum/model-flags" = local.cfg_checksum
    }
  }
  data = {
    flags = local.flags_json
  }
}
resource "kubernetes_deployment" "svc" {
  metadata { name = var.deployment }
  spec {
    template {
      metadata {
        annotations = {
          "checksum/model-flags" = kubernetes_config_map.model_flags.metadata[0].annotations["checksum/model-flags"]
        }
      }
      ...
    }
  }
}
```
Infra SRE: that avoids awkward kubectl patch hacks.
Maya Chen: thanks — copying that snippet into PR. I computed md5 in TF locals like above.
Lucia Gomez: question about secrets: the ConfigMap contains some non-sensitive knobs and a pointer to sealed secret for API keys. we should avoid embedding any creds.
Maya Chen: agreed — using sealed-secrets. TF will create a kubernetes_manifest for the SealedSecret (sealedsecrets controller manages unseal).
Cheng Li: CI failing on the PR — lint errors on jsonencode ordering. @Maya Chen can you rerun fmt?
Maya Chen: on it. will push a fix in a few mins.
deploy-bot: deploy pipeline triggered for infra/pr-421 — plan started :hourglass_flowing_sand:
Samir Patel: small nit: add owner label to each ConfigMap so we can garbage collect old per-model CM in scripts.
Maya Chen: added owner label and grouping logic. pushed change at 1801234580. PTAL.
Cheng Li: LGTM from infra side, one comment about lifecycle ignore_changes if someone wants manual edits — left review.
Infra SRE: approved the checksum rollout approach. watch rollout percentages during initial push, recommend canary 5% -> 30% -> 100% using our rollout tool.
Maya Chen: great, will follow the canary plan during deploy. thanks all :pray:
deploy-bot: infra/pr-421 plan finished — no diffs for prod-approved resources.
Maya Chen: merging now. will post follow-up metrics after canary completes.
